WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.936
 
&gt;&gt; AND NOW, GOING TO CHARLESTON

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:06.339
WHERE THE COMMUNITY IS WAITING,
AND WE HAVE MIGUEL MARQUEZ THERE,

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.576
AND THE HIGH TIDE JUST AS THE
HURRICANE IS SET TO COME ASHORE,

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:13.179
AND WHAT ARE YOU SEEING?
&gt;&gt; YEAH, IT IS PRETTY MISERABLE

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.515
RIGHT NOW, AND THIS IS THE WORST
THAT WE HAVE SEEN.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:19.785
THE WINDS ARE REALLY STARTING TO
DUST UP, AND YOU CAN SEE THAT

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:21.754
RAIN COMING IN, AND PUSHED BY
THE WIND.

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:25.291
WHEN IT IS STARTS TO HURT YOUR
FACE AND FEEL IT THROUGH THE

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:28.060
CLOTHING, YOU KNOW IT IS BAD.
THIS IS WHAT SOME OF THE BAY IS

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:33.533
LOOKING LIKE, AND THE TIDE IS
NOT EXPECTED TO BE AS HIGH AS

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:40.006
THEY THOUGHT EARLIER.
IT IS FORECAST TO BE OVER 9 FEET

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:45.178
TODAY, BUT THEY ARE BELIEVING IT
IS GOING TO BE 7 1/2 FEET.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:49.182
ONE BIT FOR CHARLESTON, IT IS
LOOKING LIKE THE STORM IS GOING

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:54.621
TO PASS TO THE EAST, AND IT IS
GOING TO PUSH IT OUT MORE INTO

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:58.491
THE OCEAN, SO THIS STREET IS
BLOCKED OUT HERE, AND SOME FOLKS

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:05.165
ARE OUT AND ABOUT, AND THIS IS
NOT A TERRIBLE STORM FOR CH

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:09.636
CHARLESTON SO FAR, AND THERE IS
POWER OUT TO SOME PEOPLE IN

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:12.705
DIFFERENT AREAS, BUT IT IS LOW
COUNTRY, SO THEY ARE USED TO IT.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:16.442
THEY ARE NOT EXPECTING ANYTHING
CERTAINLY AS BAD AS FLORIDA HAS

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:19.412
SEEN, BUT THEY ARE ON ALERT.
RIGHT NOW, IT IS SOME OF THE

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:22.682
WORST OF IT.
THEY ARE EXPECTING THAT THEY MAY

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:25.885
SEE SOME FLOODING IN THIS AREA,
AND OTHER PARTS OF CHARLESTON,

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:30.924
BUT RIGHT NOW, EVERYTHING IS IN
PLACE TO DEAL WITH THIS STORM.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:34.827
CLEARLY THE WIND IS PICKING UP
RIGHT NOW, AND THEY ARE GOING TO

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:37.497
WAIT IT OUT.
THEY ARE ASKING PEOPLE TO STAY

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:41.501
HOME, AND ENJOY THE DAY IN THE
WARMTH OF YOUR OWN HOME.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:46.572
&gt;&gt; AND MIGUEL, IF YOU CAN HEAR
ME, AND IF FOR ANY REASON THAT

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:50.210
YOU NEED TO GO, PLEASE DO SO,
AND CHARLESTON IS USED TO

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:56.583
ROUTINE FLOODING AFTER HEAVY
RAIN, AND IF FOR SOME REASON

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:59.519
COMPLACENCY SETS IN AND WE WILL
RIDE IT OUT LIKE THE LAST ONE,

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:01.921
WHAT IS YOUR SENSE?
&gt;&gt; IT IS ALWAYS A FEAR, BUT

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:05.992
BECAUSE OF HOW HARD THIS STORM
HIT FLORIDA, PEOPLE ARE ON A

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:10.630
HIGHER ALERT.
THEY HAVE BEEN WATCHING FOR MUCH

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.432
OF THE DAY.
THIS IS THE WORST OF WHAT WE

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:16.102
HAVE SEEN IN THIS STORM SO FAR.
WE DO SEE A FEW PEOPLE COMING

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.337
DOWN HERE TO SORT OF LOOK
AROUND.

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:23.242
BUT THE WATER HAS NOT COME UP
NEARLY AS QUICKLY AS THEY

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:30.883
THOUGHT IT WOULD, AND SO FAR,
CHARLESTON SEEMS TO BE DOING

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:36.489
OKAY, BUT WE SEEM TO BE IN THE
WORST OF THE STORM THAT

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.324
CHORCHORLZ
T

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.859
-- CHARLESTON IS GOING TO BE
SEEING.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:43.196
&gt;&gt; AND THANK YOU, MIGUEL
MARQUEZ.

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:47.600
AND WE HAVE CHAD MYERS STANDING
BY, AND YOU HAVE SEEN MIGUEL

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.603
MARQUEZ THERE, AND YOU HAVE BEEN
THROUGH IT TIME AFTER TIME AFTER

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:53.106
TIME, AND HE IS TALKING ABOUT
THE RAIN COMING IN SIDEWAYS.

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.675
WHERE IS HE IN TERMS OF THE
ENCOUNTER WITH IAN?

00:02:55.675 --> 00:03:00.079
&gt;&gt; HE IS JUST TO THE WEST OF IAN
WHICH IS LIKELY SAVED DAMAGES IN

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:03.349
MILLIONS OF DOLLARS FOR
CHARLESTON, BECAUSE THE 5:00

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:08.454
A.M. FORECAST WAS FOR THE SURGE,
THE TIDE TO GET TO 9 FEET.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:12.158
CHARLESTON IS FLOODING AT 6 1/2,
AND SO YES, WE WILL FLOOD AT A

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:16.329
FOOT, BUT NOT 2 1/2 FEET INTO
ALL OF THE HOMES REALLY IN THE

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:18.631
DOWNTOWN.
SOME SANDBAGS CAN TAKE CARE OF

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.867
THAT.
IT IS STILL AN 85-MILE-AN-HOUR

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:24.103
STORM, AP IT IS STILL GOING TO
BE MOVING IN SHORE OF THE LOW

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:27.840
COUNTRY OF SOUTH CAROLINA AND
LIKELY CLOSE TO GEORGETOWN AND

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.078
BIG CITY AND BIG TOWN RIGHT
THERE ALONG THE MARSHES THOUGH,

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:35.515
SO AS THE RAIN IS CONTINUING TO
COME IN AND PUSHES THE WATER IN,

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:47.460
AND I HAVE BEEN LOOKIING AT THE
MERLES ISLANDS, AND THE GOATS

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.763
ARE APPARENTLY NOT AS HARD TO
EVACUATE AS PEOPLE.

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:53.866
THEY GOT RIGHT IN.
AND SO, SOME OF THIS IS GOING TO

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:58.604
BE FLOODING FOR 4 TO 6 INCHES OF
RAIN AND PUT DOWN 2 TO 3 FEET

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:02.842
WORTH OF SURGE IN PARTS OF NORTH
CAROLINA, AND THAT IS SOMETHING

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:06.245
TO BE CONCERNED WITH.
AND THE WINDS WILL GUST INTO

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:08.915
HURRICANE STRENGTH FROM MYRTLE
BEACH TO GARDEN CITY ALL OF THE

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:12.151
WAY TO CHERRY GROVE.
HERE IS THE WINDFIELD BLOWING

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:16.422
AGAIN, AND IT IS GOING TO BE
BLOWING INTO THE CAROLINAS AND

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:20.560
GET THE TREES DOWN INTO VIRGINIA
FOR SURE LIKELY, AND BELIEVE IT

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.663
OR NOT, JOHN, THIS IS GOING TO
START TO RAIN IN NEW YORK CITY

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:27.133
TOMORROW MORNING, AND IT IS
GOING TO BE ALL OF THE WAY NORTH

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.335
HERE.
THIS IS THE LATEST FORECAST BY

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:34.707
THE RADAR MOVING UP FROM RALEIGH
TO SHORT, AND WHEN THE CELLS GET

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:39.112
HERE, THERE IS WIND 40 TO 50
MILES PER HOUR FROM NORTH

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:47.387
CAROLINA, VIRGINIA AND POSSIBLY
UP TO INTO, MARYLAND, VIRGINIA,

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:50.456
DELMARVA AND WITH THE BIGGER
CELLS THE WIND WILL COME IN.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:54.794
AND ANOTHER THING TO SHOW YOU,
EARTH CAM FROM MYRTLE BEACH.

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:58.631
EARLIER, THE TIDE IS WAY OUT
HERE, AND NOW WITH THE HIGH TIDE

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.800
AND THE SURGE RIGHT UP TO THE
MARSH AND I HAVE BEEN LOOKING AT

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:05.605
THE PICTURES COMING IN FROM SURF
SIDE, AND COMING IN FROM GARDEN

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:08.774
CITY, THE WATER IN THE STREETS
RIGHT NOW, OVER THE TOP OF THE

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:11.744
DUNES, BECAUSE THE DUNES DOWN
THERE IN THE LOWER PART OF THE

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:15.515
LOW COUNTRY OF THE GRAND STRAND
A LOT LOWER DOWN THERE, AND THE

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:18.084
WATER IS OVER THE TOP OF SOME OF
THOSE DUNES.

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:24.223
&gt;&gt; CHAD, A LITTLE PERSPECTIVE,
AND LET ME ASK YOU, WHEN IT HIT

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:27.293
SOUTHWESTERN FLORIDA, AND WE
HAVE ALL OF THE HEAVY DAMAGE OF

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:30.263
SANIBEL, AND YOU HAVE THE
DIFFERENT COAST, THE JAGGED

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:33.499
COAST OF THE ATLANTIC, AND NOW
ON THE OTHER SIDE, AND IT HAS

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.968
CROSSED THE FLORIDA PENINSULA,
BUT YOU HAVE MORRIS ISLAND TO

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:39.305
THE SOUTH, AND THE ISLAND OF
PALMS GOING UP, AND THE INLETS

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:41.908
AND THE RIVERS AND HOW DOES IT
COMPLICATE THINGS?

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:45.812
DOES THAT AREA HELP TO PROTECT
THE COAST OR DOES THE WATER

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:48.281
RESUPPLY POTENTIALLY DAMAGING TO
THE COAST?

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:52.385
&gt;&gt; DUE TO THE FACT THAT PEOPLE
BUILD ALONG THE INTERCOASTAL,

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:58.724
WATER IS COMING IN FROM THE
OTHER SIDE, AND SO, YES, IT DOES

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:00.593
HELP
HELP, BUT YOU HAVE TO STAY AWAY

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:05.932
AND AS THE PEOPLE WHO WANT TO
LIVE BY THE WATER, NOT BUILD SO

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:06.799
CLOSE.
&gt;&gt; THANK YOU, CHAD.

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:10.570
WE WILL KEEP YOU CLOSE
THROUGHOUT THE NEXT FEW HOURS

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:14.974
AND THROUGH THE WEEKEND.
&gt;&gt;&gt; AND AS SOUTH CAROLINA IS

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:21.046
WAITING, FLORIDA IS SUFFERING.
OUR JOHN BERMAN TOOK TOUR IN

00:06:21.046 --> 00:06:24.150
PLACES WHERE BUSINESSES STOOD
JUST DAYS AGO.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:27.720
&gt;&gt; ALL OF THE DEBRIS IS LITTERED
EVERYWHERE.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:31.190
THIS WERE BUILDINGS RIGHT THERE?
&gt;&gt; THERE WERE BUILDINGS,

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.961
RESTAURANTS AND WHAT USED TO BE
THE FORT MYERS PIER.

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:37.463
THE EMPTY SPOTS THERE WERE
HOMES.

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:44.370
&gt;&gt; I AM SORRY, SO THESE, THESE
ON THIS BEACH HERE, THIS WERE

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.639
HOMES?
&gt;&gt; THESE EMPTY LOTS, RIGHT

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:52.378
THERE, THOSE LOTS WERE HOMES.
THOSE WERE HOTELS, AND THOSE

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:58.618
WERE REAL PROPERTY, TWO, THREE,
FOUR OR FIVE-STORIES HIGH WASHED

00:06:58.618 --> 00:07:01.654
AWAY.
&gt;&gt; RANDI KAYE IS THERE IN FORT

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:05.925
MYERS, FLORIDA, AND RANDI, IT IS
DEVASTATING TO SEE JOHN BERMAN'S

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:09.328
VIEW FROM ABOVE, AND YOU ARE AT
THE GROUND LEVEL AND SEEING MORE

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:12.732
OF IT.
&gt;&gt; YES, WE CERTAINLY ARE, JOHN.

00:07:12.732 --> 00:07:17.503
WE ARE AT FORT MYERS BEACH AND
JUST BEHIND ME, YOU ARE SEEING

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:22.308
WHAT WE HAVE SEEN ALONG THE WAY,
AND CAPTAIN TONY'S FISHING

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:26.879
ADVENTURES IS A POPULAR TOURISM
BOAT, AND MEANWHILE, IT IS ON

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:29.949
GROUND, AND PUSHED OUT OF THE
GULF AND ON TO DRYLAND.

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:32.818
YOU CAN SEE THAT THERE IS
ANOTHER BOAT BEHIND IT, THE

00:07:32.818 --> 00:07:36.222
SMALLER BOAT, AND THE TRAILER,
AND THE SMALLER BOAT WAS ON THE

00:07:36.222 --> 00:07:39.659
TRAILER, AND ALL OF IT WAS
PUSHED ON TO DRY LAND, AND THEN

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:43.296
THERE'S A COUPLE OF OTHER BOATS
BEHIND THERE, AND BOTH OF THEM

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:46.832
ARE 50 TONS, ACTUALLY.
WE SPOKE TO THE OWNER, AND THIS

00:07:46.832 --> 00:07:50.703
IS HIS BUSINESS AND IT WAS LIKE
A FLOATING HOTEL, AND HE

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:53.973
ACTUALLY RODE THE STORM OUT ON
ONE OF THE BOATS WHICH NOW HAS A

00:07:53.973 --> 00:08:00.513
GIANT HOLE IN IT, AND HE WAS ON
IT AS HE WAS CARRIED TO DRYLAND,

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:03.616
AND WE SPOKE TO HIM EARLIER.
&gt;&gt; IT WAS WINDY AND A LOT OF

00:08:03.616 --> 00:08:06.886
RAIN OBVIOUSLY.
IT WASN'T JUST -- WE HELD OUR

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:11.524
OWN FOR A LONG TIME UNTIL ABOUT
3:00 OR SO, AND WE KEPT THE BOAT

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:14.961
IN THE SLIP WITH THE ENGINES AND
THEN THE TIDE CAME HIGH EAR AND

00:08:14.961 --> 00:08:18.831
THE WINDS REALLY RAMPED UP, AND
THE BOAT RELEASE AND WE CRUISED

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:23.869
ACROSS THE PARKING LOT.
&gt;&gt; HE SAID IT WAS INCREDIBLE,

00:08:23.869 --> 00:08:27.506
AND HE WAS NOT THAT SCARED
BECAUSE THE BOAT WAS MADE OF

00:08:27.506 --> 00:08:31.377
STEEL, AND HE DIDN'T FEEL THAT
THE STORM WOULD THAT BE BAD, BUT

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:35.281
HE SAW THE BUILDINGS COLLAPSE
INTO THE WATER, AND OTHERS THAT

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:38.150
HAD BEEN IN DRY LAND.
AND THIS IS ALSO WHAT WE ARE

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:41.253
FINDING A MARINA THAT IS NOW
SHATTERED AND RESTAURANTS THAT

00:08:41.253 --> 00:08:44.090
ARE SHATTERED.
WE SAW BOATS THAT ARE BASICALLY

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:47.593
THAT HAVE BEEN TOSSED AROUND
LIKE TOYS IN THE TREES AND ON

00:08:47.593 --> 00:08:50.563
THE SIDE OF THE ROAD.
THERE IS A BUNCH OF TWISTED

00:08:50.563 --> 00:08:53.833
METAL AND BOATS DOWN THERE, AND
WE ARE NOT FAR FROM THE GULF.

00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:58.237
IF WE WENT THIS WAY, WE WOULD GO
RIGHT ON TO THE ACTUAL BEACH OF

00:08:58.237 --> 00:09:00.940
FORT MYERS WHICH JOHN BERMAN WAS
FLYING OVER.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:04.510
THERE IS SO MUCH DESTRUCTION AND
SO MUCH DEBRIS IN THE ROAD THAT

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.879
THEY ARE TURNING PEOPLE BACK,
JOHN.

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:10.750
THIS IS JUST ONE EXAMPLE OF
SOMEBODY IN HIS STORY TO TELL

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:14.520
THAT WE ARE SEEING ALONG THE WAY
HERE IN FORT MYERS BEACH.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:21.560
&gt;&gt; BEFORE I LET YOU GO, RANDI, I
WILL WANT TO GET YOUR

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:24.530
PERSPECTIVE BECAUSE OF YOUR
EXPERIENCE AND GOING OUT TO

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:28.601
BARRIER ISLAND AND THE CAUSEWAY
DESTROYED AND THE PICTURES

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:31.604
COMING IN, AND WHETHER IT IS
SANIBEL OR WHERE YOU ARE IN FORT

00:09:31.604 --> 00:09:35.274
MYERS AND DAY ONE, DO WE NEED TO
FIND PEOPLE AND RESCUE PEOPLE,

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:38.644
AND THE DAY TWO IS WHOA, AS YOU
ARE LOOKING AT THE DEVASTATION

00:09:38.644 --> 00:09:42.415
AND TRYING TO HAVE SOME CONTEXT
AND THEN YOU TRY TO ADD IT UP,

00:09:42.415 --> 00:09:45.851
HOW LONG WILL IT TAKE, AND HOW
MUCH DOES IT COST, AND WHEN CAN

00:09:45.851 --> 00:09:49.755
I GO HOME IF MY HOUSE IS NO
LONGER THERE, AND WHAT DO YOU

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:50.589
SEE?
&gt;&gt; ABSOLUTELY.

00:09:50.589 --> 00:09:54.160
AND WE HAVE SEEN THIS STEADY
STREAM OF TRAFFIC WHICH IS

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.163
PRETTY REMARKABLE, BECAUSE THEY
ARE ALL BEING TURNED AWAY WHEN

00:09:57.163 --> 00:09:59.699
THEY GET TO THE BEACH.
SOME OF THEM ARE CURIOUS PEOPLE,

00:09:59.699 --> 00:10:04.704
AND THEY WANT TO SEE SOME OF THE
DAMAGE, BUT SOME OF THEM ARE THE

00:10:04.704 --> 00:10:07.106
HOMEOWNERS TO WANT TO GO SEE
WHAT IS GOING ON WITH THE HOMES

00:10:07.106 --> 00:10:11.677
AND WHAT IS LEFT OF THEM
CERTAINLY AT FORT MYERS BEACH,

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:14.714
AND THE BOAT OWNER, AND THE
POWER COMPANY CAME BY, AND THE

00:10:14.714 --> 00:10:18.484
POWER LINES ARE WHAT STOPPED HIS
BOAT FROM GOING FURTHER TO WHERE

00:10:18.484 --> 00:10:21.687
WE ARE ACROSS THE STREET.
SO HE IS SITTING ON POWER LINES.

00:10:21.687 --> 00:10:24.990
SO THERE IS SO MUCH WORK TO BE
DONE AND SO MANY QUESTIONS FROM

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:27.593
PEOPLE ABOUT WHAT IS NEXT, JOHN.

